        {
          "id": "apn-note",
          "type": "note",
          "kind": "Note",
          "title": "Source and limits of this reproduction",
          "state": "ready",
          "x": 80,
          "y": 530,
          "note": {
            "text": "Reproduces the computational protocol of Molecules 2024, 29(8), 1808 (open access, CC BY 4.0): structures optimized with DFT/B3LYP/6-311++G(d,p) in Gaussian 16, vibrational analysis to confirm a minimum, then TD-DFT with five singlet excited states at the same level in the PCM solvent model, for toluene, THF, DCM, DMSO and methanol. Targets reported for compound 1 in methanol and DMSO: 408.18 nm (3.037 eV, f = 0.640) and ~309 nm (4.009 eV, f = 0.412). No result is claimed for those targets here: this project prepares the inputs, and the paper does not state the cavity/dispersion settings or the optimization solvent, which are left at Gaussian defaults and flagged in the reproduction notes."
          }
        }
